# /{{word}} — this harness's word for adding a {{flow_file}}

Scaffolded once by /the-world:start from this harness's `WORLD.md` Vocabulary table, so
that this world's own word is a real command rather than narration.

Read `WORLD.md` for the cast, the vocabulary, and the naming pool, and `docs/philosophy.md`
for why each boundary in this kit exists. Then add the {{flow_file}} the user asked for,
keeping what already holds for every other one here: authority declared in code and narrow,
`write_scope` no wider than the work (empty, which writes nothing, for one that only reads),
a scoped tool rather than a wider Bash allowlist, outward actions behind human approval, and
a report that says what is still unverified. Keep speaking in {{universe_name}}'s vocabulary.

Anything the new code posts to Slack by itself is built with `world.slack.blocks.card(title,
fields=..., bullets=..., body=..., context=..., buttons=...)` and posted with
`listener.post(text, blocks=blocks)`: a headline with the outcome, one fact per field or
bullet, ids and paths in backticks, context last. Not a hand-built line joining facts with
commas.

This wrapper is yours. If `WORLD.md`'s Vocabulary entry changes, rename this skill's folder
(the directory holding this `SKILL.md`) to match — it is a one-time scaffold, not read from
`WORLD.md` at runtime.
